### Sponge Project Structure Map

Use this as a navigation guide for this repo. The main entry for the CLI is
[cmd/sponge/main.go](mdc:cmd/sponge/main.go). It initializes commands from
[cmd/sponge/commands](mdc:cmd/sponge/commands).

- **APIs and Protobuf**
  - Protos live under [api/](mdc:api/). Example service: [api/serverNameExample/v1/userExample.proto](mdc:api/serverNameExample/v1/userExample.proto).
  - Generated files are co-located: `*_pb.go`, `*_grpc.pb.go`, `*_pb.validate.go`, and router stubs like `*_router.pb.go`.

- **Service Code (monolith-style layout)**
  - Entrypoint server binary: [cmd/serverNameExample_mixExample/main.go](mdc:cmd/serverNameExample_mixExample/main.go)
    with initialization in [cmd/serverNameExample_mixExample/initial](mdc:cmd/serverNameExample_mixExample/initial).
  - HTTP/GRPC servers: [internal/server](mdc:internal/server).
  - HTTP routing: [internal/routers](mdc:internal/routers), handlers in [internal/handler](mdc:internal/handler).
  - GRPC services: [internal/service](mdc:internal/service).
  - Config structs: [internal/config](mdc:internal/config), config files in [configs/](mdc:configs/).
  - Data access and models: [internal/dao](mdc:internal/dao), [internal/model](mdc:internal/model), DB init in [internal/database](mdc:internal/database).
  - Error codes: [internal/ecode](mdc:internal/ecode).

- **Shared Libraries**
  - Shared packages live under [pkg/](mdc:pkg/), such as Gin helpers, GRPC, JWT, logger, etc.

- **Build/Deploy/Docs**
  - Make targets: [Makefile](mdc:Makefile). Local run script: [scripts/run.sh](mdc:scripts/run.sh).
  - Protobuf/codegen scripts: [scripts/protoc.sh](mdc:scripts/protoc.sh), proto docs: [scripts/proto-doc.sh](mdc:scripts/proto-doc.sh).
  - Swagger generation: [scripts/swag-docs.sh](mdc:scripts/swag-docs.sh), docs in [docs/](mdc:docs/).
  - Deployment manifests: [deployments/docker-compose](mdc:deployments/docker-compose), [deployments/kubernetes](mdc:deployments/kubernetes).

Tip: Prefer navigating to `internal/*` for runtime behavior, `cmd/*` for entrypoints,
`api/*` for definitions, and `pkg/*` for reusable utilities.

